todo!() for dom/cod/@ in algebraize::walk_term

The Dom/Cod/MorApp branches in walk_term no longer materialise a
fresh untyped El. That was wrong in the absence of proper operator
support, so collapse all three into a single `todo!()` branch with
a TODO comment explaining the gap.

Fallout:

- 4 compile tests exercising these operators are marked `#[ignore]`
  with a matching reason:
    non_mor_applied_as_mor
    mor_applied_to_non_member
    mor_applied_to_false_member
    surjectivity_violation_mor_app

- 5 eval `.eql` files that use dom/cod/@ are deactivated by renaming
  to `.eql.deactivated` (matching the existing convention used by
  indexed_set_with_total_mors.eql.deactivated). The corresponding
  `eqlog_mod!` entries and `#[cfg(test)] mod ..._test;` lines in
  eqlog-test-eval/src/lib.rs are commented out with the same reason.
  Affected: indexed_abelian_group, inference, lex_category,
  product_category, subset_rules.

Tests: 42/46 compile (4 ignored), 53/73 eval (20 gone with the
deactivated modules).
